# switches-off.vrs: feature switches bind admins, and cleanup still works with the feature off.
# Needs config: ObjectSpawn.Enabled=false, CastleEvents.DoorGates=false, PublicStorage.CostsEnabled=false (everything
# else on), and at least one Uriel object on plot 11 (spawned before the restart, e.g. by switches-setup.vrs).
# Plot 11 layout gate1/gate2 (both bound to doors) + template evtest (castle-event.vrs).
ensure
console TPHome
wait 3
mark
chat .uriel features
expect-reply Object spawning OFF.
expect-seen \[CHAT> ${CHARACTER}\] Uriel features:.*event doors OFF\. Public chests on, prison cells on, paid shares OFF\.
# object spawning is off for an admin too, and for the Raphael api
chat .devtp -2030 -1717 5
wait 3
chat .uriel spawn TM_Glassblower_Crate01 here
expect-reply Object spawning is disabled by the server admin (ObjectSpawn.Enabled).
chat .uriel api version
expect-reply [URIEL:err] code=disabled
# doors: binding and the door tool are refused; a run leaves every door alone
chat .devtp -2030 -1713 5
wait 2
chat .uriel event door gate1
expect-reply Event doors are disabled by the server admin (CastleEvents.DoorGates).
chat .uriel unit door show
expect-reply Event doors are disabled by the server admin (CastleEvents.DoorGates).
chat .devtp -2014 -1705 5
wait 3
chat .uriel event start evtest
expect-log \[Uriel EVENT\] started territory=11 template=evtest groups=2 units=3 bosses=1 doors=0 failedMarkers=0
expect-no-log \[Uriel EVENT\] door-held
chat .uriel event stop
expect-log \[Uriel EVENT\] stopped territory=11 units=3 doorsRestored=0
wait 4
# cleanup works with object spawning off
chat .devtp -2030 -1717 5
wait 3
chat .uriel purgeplot
expect-reply Uriel-spawned object(s) from this plot. Native objects were left untouched.
expect-log \[Uriel SPAWN\] purged [1-9]\d* object\(s\) \(\d+ marker \+ \d+ record\) from territory 11
chat .uriel unit list
expect-reply No Uriel units
console TPHome
